    posts: [
      { id: 'b1', slug: 'component-spec-files', order: 1, title: 'Component spec files: the 8-section template', title_ar: 'ملفات مواصفات المكوّنات: قالب من ثمانية أقسام', date: '2026-09-01', updated: true, read: '9 min read', topics: ['Design systems'],
        excerpt: 'The 8-section component spec template: metadata, overview, anatomy, tokens, props, states, code, cross-refs. Download the Markdown.',
        excerpt_ar: 'قالب مواصفات المكوّن من ثمانية أقسام: البيانات الوصفية، النظرة العامة، التشريح، الرموز، الخصائص، الحالات، الشيفرة، المراجع. نزّل ملف Markdown.',
        lead: 'A design system is only as good as the file an engineer, or an AI agent, opens at 11pm. This is the structure I use so that file is the same every time.',
        download: { label: 'Download the template (.md)', href: '../assets/downloads/component-spec-template.md' }, cover: '',
        body: [
          { h: 'Why a spec file, not a Figma page', p: ['Figma shows what a component looks like. It doesn\u2019t say which token a border reads, what happens on disabled, or which other components break when the padding changes. Engineers rebuild from screenshots, AI agents guess, and three months later you have four buttons.', 'A spec file is plain Markdown that lives next to the code. It is small enough to read in two minutes and structured enough that a model can be pointed at it and produce on-system UI.'] },
          { h: 'Six tiers of files', tiers: [['Foundations', 'colour, spacing, typography, radius, elevation, motion.'], ['Token reference', 'the master map of every CSS variable, primitive to semantic to component.'], ['Atoms', 'button, input, icon-button, badge. One spec each.'], ['Molecules and organisms', 'composed components specific to your product.'], ['Patterns', 'layout rules, content flow and spacing between elements.'], ['Cross-references', '"uses" and "used by" links across all files.']] },
          { h: 'The 8-section template', grid: [['Metadata', 'Name, tier, status, owner, version, last reviewed.'], ['Overview', 'What it is for, when to use it, when not to.'], ['Anatomy', 'Named parts, slots and their order.'], ['Tokens', 'Every variable the component reads, never a raw value.'], ['Props / API', 'Name, type, default, required, and the design intent behind each.'], ['States', 'Rest, hover, focus-visible, active, disabled, loading, error, with contrast noted.'], ['Code examples', 'The three most common compositions, copy-pasteable.'], ['Cross-refs', 'Uses / used by, so a change shows its blast radius.']] },
          { h: 'A skeleton you can copy', code: '# button.md\n\n## 01 Metadata\ntier: atom · status: stable · owner: design-systems · v2.3\n\n## 02 Overview\nPrimary action. One per view. Not for navigation.\n\n## 04 Tokens\nbackground   --action-primary\nlabel        --text-on-brand\nradius       --radius-pill\n\n## 06 States\nhover → --action-primary-hover · focus-visible → --shadow-focus\n\n## 08 Cross-refs\nuses: icon · used by: hero, dialog-footer, form-actions' },
          { h: 'How AI agents use it', p: ['Point the model at the token reference and the spec for the component it needs. Because sections 04 and 06 are explicit, the agent has no reason to invent a hex code or skip the focus state.'] },
          { h: 'Before you publish a spec', list: ['Every value in section 04 is a token name, not a number.', 'Section 06 lists focus-visible and reduced-motion behaviour, with contrast ratios.', 'The code example renders in Storybook without edits.', 'Cross-refs are reciprocal: if A uses B, B lists A under "used by".'] }] }
    ],
